            <div class="panel-head"><span>Deepnest-next</span><b>43 / 61</b></div>
            <div class="layout-stage" tabindex="0" aria-label="Deepnest-next supplied export. Use zoom buttons or plus and minus keys; drag to pan when zoomed."><div class="drawing" set:html={svg('deepnest-next')}></div></div>
            <div class="panel-foot"><span>43-part export checkpoint</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="layout-panel" data-layout="deepnest" hidden>
            <div class="panel-head"><span>Deepnest</span><b class="warn">55 / 61 <small>UI-reported</small></b></div>
            <div class="layout-stage" tabindex="0" aria-label="Deepnest supplied export, including open fragments. Use zoom buttons or plus and minus keys; drag to pan when zoomed."><div class="drawing" set:html={svg('deepnest')}></div></div>
            <div class="panel-foot"><span>49 complete parts; fragments left open</span><span class="warn">5+ intersecting pairs</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption id="layout-note" aria-live="polite">Placement density comparison. Kenzap Nesting on the left; <span id="layout-competitor">Deepnest-next</span> on the right.</figcaption>
        <noscript><p class="micro">The interactive viewer needs JavaScript. <a href={`${base}/deepnest.svg`}>View the original Deepnest layout</a> or download the DXFs at the end of this article.</p></noscript>
      </figure>

      <div class="body">
        <h2>The files, if you'd like to check</h2>
        <p>I've kept the original exports unchanged. Download them and open them in your CAD viewer; the measurements and test notes are here too.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="body downloads">
        {[kenzap, next, deepnest].map((result) => <div class="download-row"><div><strong>{result.name}</strong><span>{result.parts === null ? '49 complete parts + 12 open fragments' : `${result.parts} complete parts`} · {(result.fileBytes / 1024).toFixed(0)} KB</span><details><summary>SHA-256</summary><code>{result.sha256}</code></details></div><a class="download-link" href={`${base}/${result.file}`} download>Download DXF <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5M4 17v4h16v-4" /></svg></a></div>)}
        <p class="evidence-links"><a href={`${base}/analysis.json`} download>Raw analysis (JSON)</a><a href={`${base}/README.md`} download>Test record</a><a href={`${base}/benchmark-exports.zip`} download>Everything (ZIP)</a></p>
        <p class="micro">The original input DXF is not included, so these files let you check the outputs but not yet reproduce the runs end to end.</p>

